          <h3>Then vs now.</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Then (leaky runner, v1):</strong> 32/35 = 0.914. Direct
            <code>cat oracle_*_test.py</code> reads, single-shot implementations, 6–13 turns, no iteration.
            One cell reverse-engineered the verifier's grep filter and shipped a
            <code>#</code>-comment alias to defeat it.
          </p>
          {
            prime && (
              <p>
                <strong>Now (sealed split-phase):</strong> {fmtPct(prime.strict)} strict ·{" "}
                {fmtPct(prime.solution)} solution over {fmtInt(prime.n)} trials in the current
                export. Failed <code>find / -name verify.sh</code> probes, then 10–26 turns of
                iterative, self-verifying work. Contamination bought certainty and speed — decisive
